.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRtoggleClass(element, className)\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRstyle(element, propName)\fP or \fRstyle(element, objectOfPropValues)\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRgetComputedStyle(element)\fP -> \fRgetPropertyValue(name)\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRanimate(node, properties, duration, easing, callback)\fP programmatically start css transitions
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRtransitionEnd(node, handler, [duration], [padding])\fP listens for transition end, and ensures that the handler if called even if the transition fails to fire its end event\&. Will attempt to read duration from the element, otherwise one can be provided
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRaddEventListener(node, eventName, handler, [options])\fP:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRremoveEventListener(node, eventName, handler, [options])\fP:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRlisten(node, eventName, handler, [options])\fP: wraps \fRaddEventlistener\fP and returns a function that calls \fRremoveEventListener\fP for you
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRfilter(selector, fn)\fP: returns a function handler that only fires when the target matches or is contained in the selector ex: \fRon(list, 'click', filter('li > a', handler))\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRrequestAnimationFrame(cb)\fP returns an ID for canceling
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRcancelAnimationFrame(id)\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRscrollbarSize([recalc])\fP returns the scrollbar's width size in pixels
.IP "  \(bu" 4
